{
  "note": "Captured from the Go core (backend/runtimes/cli serve) on a fresh temporary database and replayed against the Rust core by the local_core test. Volatile fields listed in `masked` are replaced by <masked> on both sides. Two differences are recorded rather than compared: a stream fixture lists the frames the Go core sent before the capture cut the live stream, while the port answers the same frames and ends the stream (incremental delivery needs a futures_core stream, absent from core/Cargo.toml); and the Go core's Accept-Post on a 415 lists the protobuf and gRPC codecs, which the port does not speak.",
  "token": "test-session-token",
  "masked": [
    "at",
    "createdAt",
    "updatedAt",
    "archivedAt",
    "uptimeSec",
    "pid",
    "build"
  ],
  "cases": [
